  "findings": [
    "Java has no independent return painter: CommandReturn produces Message and MessageArrow#getLeftStartInternal/getRightEndInternal samples the spatial left/right live segments. Rust ordinary-return lowering correctly shares sequence_arrow_endpoints and the message constraints; eight fresh nested delegated-return cases pass across direction/order/label and both engines.",
    "Both fresh explicit-color return cases fail: CommandReturn applies COLOR to the inherited dotted configuration; ReturnMessage currently retains it as visible label text and the normalized message does not override arrow color. Legacy interparticipant canvas is316px versus369px. Whole-source return semantics therefore remain rejected even though the endpoint algebra has positive evidence.",
    "No regression of any previously passing parent955 or maker535 input was found. Correct internal endpoint selection does not waive unresolved parser/lifecycle dependencies.",
    "All14 accounts were present byte-for-byte in earlier chronological commits before their corresponding code. See provenance.json and commit-mapping.json. Main release tiers remain11181/11251 product-library and10497/11251 assisted-library; source-only CLI cohort403/955 with10 invalid references; no regressions observed.",
    "Verdict applies to whole source-to-SVG recovery with the dependencies described above. Positive component-local observations are explicitly bounded and are not acceptance. Every mismatch and negative remains in the standing suite."
  ],
